I fixed #1075 in commit 290f7308. The Fixes #1075 title closes the issue when this is pushed. The tree hasn't been pushed yet.

What changed
• run_doctor_checks and handle_doctor (in src/commands_dev.rs) now take a new DoctorSurface { Repl, Shell } argument. Shell yoyo doctor passes Shell; REPL /doctor passes Repl. Only the call arguments changed in src/dispatch_sub.rs (+1 line) and src/dispatch.rs, and the module-size gate is still green.
• Project-context row: the shell now says create YOYO.md or run yoyo init. The REPL text is exactly the same as before (… or run /init).
• Memory-dir row: both surfaces now say mkdir -p .yoyo to create, which is the same command /doctor offers to run right below the row. The REPL version also mentions or /remember <note>. I checked the code before adding that: saving a note creates .yoyo/ (save_memories_to calls create_dir_all). A bare /remember only prints usage, and the shell has no remember command.
• I added a short paragraph to docs/src/usage/commands.md. No doc quoted the old text, and nothing in src, docs or skills points at #1075.

Tests
• Full-string assert_eq! checks for both rows on both surfaces, including a check that the REPL context row didn't change.
• A test that the memory row contains the exact command doctor_fix_action offers.
• A test that runs the real binary: yoyo doctor in a fresh temp dir prints the shell wording and no /init or /remember.
• Positive control: I made the shell path pass Repl, and the binary test failed. Restoring it made the test pass again, all in one command.
• fmt, clippy with -D warnings, and the full cargo test (25 test binaries) all pass.

Left over: the Curl row still says /docs and /web on both surfaces. That was outside #1075's scope. The shell has yoyo docs but no web command, so I filed it as #1083 so it has a home after #1075 closes.
